Subject: [PATCH] Restore ANGLE display and resource recovery

Port the Windows ANGLE recovery from desktop-app/patches Qt 5.15.19
0033-gl-context-restore.patch and 0035-debug-gl-context-restore.patch at
f7433965ed33996c641a822c78a81eef3526c9e7. Their original commits are
446f47239df3102a9a24304b5e3a8c9bee5784f7 and
0da942abf8283add899ae783432093e5f8742a12.

Retire lost EGL displays while retaining their context/surface owners,
track and release old window surfaces, preserve the device-loss teardown
policy and recreate ANGLE with a fresh display key. Compare/exchange the
lost display's key instead of throttling key changes by time, so rapid
successive device losses cannot reuse a poisoned display and a logged
loss followed by its EGL error advances only once.

Retain Qt 6's deferred QOpenGLWidget wrapper deletion from common patch
0009, port the GL resource/FBO safeguards, and report invalid contexts
through the QRhi device-loss path. Restore the Qt 5 ANGLE extension alias
lookup and safely initialize/retire Qt 6's native EGL context wrapper.
Requires the qt6_windows7 ANGLE patches and the common Qt 6.11.2 series
(in particular 0008 and 0009). ANGLE interfaces verified against
b34c4dc879d115d34794a657c7fa5f6bb34bc10a.

